course: everyday
lesson: 478
title: Three's a crowd, and the friend who picks someone else
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lily, Maddie and Chloe are a three. On the path to school there's only room for two side by side, so someone walks behind, and lately it's always Lily, staring at two heads whispering and giggling. Finally she says, «I'm always at the back.» Maddie honestly hadn't noticed. They start taking turns, and on wide bits they walk three abreast like cowboys in a film. Threes are tricky; say how you feel before you start sulking.
explain: Sometimes a friend picks someone else. Jake starts sitting with the new boy, Zack, who has a Switch: «It's lowkey fire, bro» («lowkey fire» means quietly brilliant). Sam stops waiting at the table and goes to chess club, and by spring he has two new mates. Ava picks Hannah for the project «cos Hannah's good at drawing», and Mia is put with Oscar, who turns out to know everything about volcanoes. Their volcano erupts baking soda all over the teacher's desk; it gets the best mark in the class, and Mia has a new friend. Not being picked once is not the same as not being liked.
explain: Before deciding you were dumped, ask. Kieran sees a photo of Connor and Jake at the cinema without him. He asks them straight out; Connor goes red: «We thought you were at your dad's this weekend, mate.» Connor's best mate Raj moves to another table, and Connor spends all of maths sure he's done something wrong. «Have I done summat?» («summat» is Northern for something.) Raj looks baffled: «Nah, I just wanna sit with the Minecraft lot sometimes.»
explain: Some leaving-out is cruel. Harper hands out pool-party invitations to the whole class except Mia, right in front of her. The teacher has a quiet word with Harper's mum, and Mia's grandma takes her to the cinema «for a party of two». Aisha tells Chloe she can be her «second best friend», and Chloe feels as if she's been demoted. When Ade goes off to play with the Year 6 lads, Sam and Jake stop moping and find a bigger game with the girls from Maddie's class. And when Ellie and Jess row over a gel pen and each wants Maddie on her side, Maddie says, «I'm not picking sides, it's a pen.» Lily solves threes another way: games that need three, like piggy in the middle with turns, and on bad days they go and find a fourth.
fact: Groups of three are tricky, because two can easily pair off and leave one out.
fact: Saying calmly how you feel, such as «I'm always at the back», works better than sulking.
fact: Taking turns, or choosing games that fit three people, helps a three stay fair.
fact: When a friend spends time with someone new, you cannot force them back; doing your own things and leaving the door open helps.
fact: Not being picked once, for a project or a team, does not mean you are not liked.
fact: Being left out is sometimes just a mix-up in plans, so it is worth asking before deciding.
fact: Friends are allowed to have other friends.
fact: Leaving one person out on purpose, in front of them, is cruel; it is not their fault, and telling a grown-up is right.
fact: You do not have to take sides in someone else's row; «I'm staying out of it» is allowed.
fact: Friendships do not need rankings like «best» and «second best»; spend time with people who are glad to see you.
fact: «Lowkey» means quietly or a bit, «fire» means brilliant, and «summat» means something in the North of England.
exercise: Why does someone always walk behind on the path to school? | There's only room for two side by side | Lily likes walking alone at the back best | The others are faster | It's a school rule
exercise: What happened when Lily said «I'm always at the back»? | Maddie hadn't noticed, and they started taking turns | They stopped walking together and Lily went on her own | Maddie laughed at her | Chloe walked behind forever
exercise: Why did Jake start sitting with Zack? | Zack had a Switch | Jake hated Sam now | The teacher moved him there | Zack paid him to sit there
exercise: What did Sam do instead of waiting for Jake? | Joined chess club and made new mates | Followed Jake everywhere, even to the toilets | Told Zack to go away | Sat alone every day
exercise: Why did Ava pick Hannah for the project? | Hannah was good at drawing | Ava didn't like Mia any more | Hannah gave her sweets | The teacher made her
exercise: How did Mia's project with Oscar turn out? | Best in the class, and a new friend | A disaster they both hated working on | They never spoke once | Oscar did nothing at all
exercise: Kieran wasn't asked to the cinema. What was the real reason? | They thought he was at his dad's that weekend | They secretly hated him and wanted him out of the group | They forgot he existed | He was banned from the cinema
exercise: Aisha said Chloe could be her «second best friend». How did Chloe feel? | Like she'd been demoted | Proud to be second best | She didn't care at all really | Happy to have a new best friend
exercise: Ellie and Jess each wanted Maddie on their side. What did Maddie say? | «I'm not picking sides, it's a pen» | «I'm on Ellie's side» | «I'm on Jess's side» | «I'll never speak to either of you»
exercise: Ade started playing with the Year 6 lads. What did Sam and Jake find? | A bigger game with the girls from Maddie's class | Nobody else to play with, ever, for the rest of the year | That Ade hated them | That two-and-in was brilliant
exercise: How did Lily make threes fairer? | Games that need three, or finding a fourth | Leaving one person out each day, taking turns | Choosing the same pair every time | Telling the teacher every break
exercise: Harper invited the whole class except Mia, in front of her. What is that? | Cruel | A normal mix-up | Mia's own fault | A kind joke
exercise: What did Mia's grandma do on party day? | Took Mia to the cinema, a party of two | Went to shout at Harper's mum | Made Mia go to the party anyway | Ignored it
exercise: Raj moved to another table. What was the reason? | He wanted to sit with the Minecraft lot sometimes | He was angry with Connor about something he'd said | Connor had smelled | The teacher moved him
exercise: What does «summat» mean? | Something | Summer | Some money | Sometimes
test: «they always walk in front and I'm stuck at the back, so I'll just sulk». Better idea? | Say how you feel and suggest taking turns | Sulk till they guess | Push in between them so you're in the middle | Walk the other way forever
test: «Jake's sat with Zack again, he's a snake, I'm done with him». What's more likely true? | Jake chose something new for now, he's not an enemy | Jake is plotting against Sam with Zack behind his back | Zack paid Jake to hate Sam | Sam did something terrible
test: «Ava didn't pick me so she must hate me». Is that right? | No, not being picked once isn't being disliked | Yes, being picked shows who likes you most | Yes, best friends must always pick you first | No, Ava is just scared of Mia
test: Kieran sees the cinema photo and types «fine, be like that, ur all fake». What would have been better? | Ask them first what happened | Post a mean photo of them | Never speak to them again | Tell their mums
test: «You can be my second best friend if u want». Is ranking friends a good idea? | No, friends don't need numbers | Yes, everyone should have a list | Yes, and you should be told yours | No, you should only have one friend
test: «If you talk to her you're not my friend». What can Maddie say? | «I'm staying out of it» | «OK, I'll never talk to her» | «Then I'll pick her side» | «I'll tell everyone your secrets»
test: «Have I done summat?» Raj: «Nah, just wanna sit with the Minecraft lot». What does this show? | Friends can have other friends | Raj secretly hates Connor | Connor should be upset forever | Minecraft ruins friendships
test: Harper gives out party invites in class to everyone but one girl. What should that girl do? | Tell a grown-up and do something nice with family | Tell everyone Harper's party is rubbish and nobody should go | Steal an invite | Turn up at the party anyway
test: What would probably happen if Sam kept waiting at the lunch table every day for Jake? | He'd stay lonely and keep feeling hurt | Jake would come back the next day | Zack would leave the school | The teacher would make Jake come back
test: In a TV show, a girl left out of a party throws a bigger party for revenge. What's wiser in real life? | Spend time with people who are glad to see you | Plan an even bigger party so they all feel left out | Ruin the other party | Never go to a party again
test: «there's three of us and it's always two v one, it's giving drama». («it's giving» means it feels like.) What's a real fix? | Play games that need three, or find a fourth | Kick one person out for good | Always pick the same two | Stop being friends with both
exam: Identify the principal reason, as established in the lesson, for which friendships of three persons are prone to difficulty. | Two members may readily pair off, excluding the third | Three persons cannot converse simultaneously | Such friendships are prohibited by schools | The third member is invariably disliked
exam: Ascertain the most appropriate response of a pupil who perceives that she has been excluded from an outing by friends. | To inquire of the friends directly before forming a conclusion | To conclude immediately that she has been rejected by all of them | To denounce the friends publicly online | To terminate the friendships without inquiry
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the distribution of party invitations to all pupils of a class save one, in her presence? | It constitutes deliberate and cruel exclusion | It constitutes an innocent administrative error | It is the responsibility of the excluded pupil | It is a customary and wholly acceptable practice
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning a pupil solicited by two quarrelling friends to take a side. | She is entitled to decline to take either side | She is obliged to choose one party | She must abandon both friendships | She must refer the matter to a court
